			"description": "<p>A flash of brilliant light, sparkling spell effects, or sudden exposure to sunlight— all of these could result in a creature being dazzled.</p><ul><li><p>A dazzled creature has disadvantage on ability checks that require sight.</p></li><li><p>A dazzled creature cannot take reactions.</p></li><li><p>Creatures that are immune to being blinded are immune to being dazzled.</p></li><li><p>If this condition is inflicted by nonmagical environmental means (such as initial exposure to sunlight after being underground for an extended period of time), it persists for 1 round before dissipating.</p></li></ul>",
